   "claims": [
    "For displays and images the aspect ratio is the ratio of width to height, for example, 16:9 or 2.35:1.",
    "One method gives you the ratio as a decimal w in proportion to h=1.",
    "Divide using the formula: aspect ratio = (width / height):1 In this case width/height = 1920/1080 = 1.77777...",
    "To calculate the aspect ratio of a computer display 1920 pixels wide x 1080 pixels high as whole numbers, first find the Greatest Common Factor of 1920 and 1080.",
    "1920 / 120 = 16 1080 / 120 = 9 So the aspect ratio in whole numbers is 16:9.",
    "The aspect ratio of sceens with this ratio are commonly referred to as 16:9 or 1.7:1 or 1.78:1."
   ],
